{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1126659-looking-for-ideas-lunar-proving-ground-2e","id":1126659,"title":"Looking for ideas: Lunar proving ground (2E)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-09T05:08:01-07:00","id":1126659,"title":"Looking for ideas: Lunar proving ground (2E)","content":"I have an idea for a session I need to throw together in short order and Im looking for suggestions...<br /> <br /> An aged (not ancient, maybe 1000 y/o) Lunar becomes aware of his solar companion's return. The lunar guards some important first age macguffin that the solar seeks, but is unsure of the solars nature and does not want to hand all that macguffiny power to a would be tyrant and wants to test the mettle of the solar and her companions.<br /> <br /> The Lunar commands a level 4 lunar demesne that is quite responsive to their will, and invites the solars into the demesne to test them and ensure they are not yet entirely crazy.<br /> <br /> What tests and trials do the solars face to prove themselves opposed to tyranny and protectors of the masses?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Visit me at <a href=\"http://www.bragrman.com\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Tales of Grey</i></a> - my RPG Game-Master's blog.<br /> <br /> &quot;If only I had an enemy bigger than my apathy, I could have won&quot; - <i>I gave you all,</i> Mumford &amp; Sons","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8520-capitantypo","name":"CapitanTypo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8520_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"896"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T15:48:22-07:00","id":1128598,"title":"","content":"I just saw this post. :/ So, if it's not too late, here are my suggestions.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking something along the lines of social trials. The Lunar may believe that a good character test would be involving situations where the Solar has an opportunity to be a good Samaritan or a complete jerk. Put the Solar/s in a situation where they have the opportunity to aid someone in need. Give the target something the Solar/s want or desire or would be otherwise useful to them. See if they take advantage of the individual and take it from them, or if they aid the individual and demand compensation, or aid the individual and ask for nothing in return.<br /> <br /> You may even involve the image of the desired macguffin. Create a scenario where a person has said macguffin and would be highly inconvenienced if it were taken from him/her. How do the Solars respond? Will they try to negotiate for the illusionary macguffin or take it by force? Hope this helps!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T15:55:43-07:00","id":1128601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1126659-looking-for-ideas-lunar-proving-ground-2e?p=1128598#post1128598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just saw this post. :/ So, if it's not too late, here are my suggestions.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking something along the lines of social trials. The Lunar may believe that a good character test would be involving situations where the Solar has an opportunity to be a good Samaritan or a complete jerk. Put the Solar/s in a situation where they have the opportunity to aid someone in need. Give the target something the Solar/s want or desire or would be otherwise useful to them. See if they take advantage of the individual and take it from them, or if they aid the individual and demand compensation, or aid the individual and ask for nothing in return.<br /> <br /> You may even involve the image of the desired macguffin. Create a scenario where a person has said macguffin and would be highly inconvenienced if it were taken from him/her. How do the Solars respond? Will they try to negotiate for the illusionary macguffin or take it by force? Hope this helps!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ya this - the old lunars are canonically mainly worried about the solars being crazy. Test for crazy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly, for such a test I would throw something slightly different a solar: Kidnap him/her in the middle of the night, strip him of his clothes, dress him in rags, roll him in mud, then deposit him in a guild or realm run quarry, one run with slave labor - and now he looks like one of the slaves - and the overseer is a DB sorcerer with summoned demon guards.<br /> <br /> The test? Well, the test is &quot;what are you going to do?&quot; - will you just run away from the place? Will you try to free the slaves? Will you kill/seduce/replace/something something the DB sorcerer in charge and take over? Will you lead a slave revolt and battle the demons? <br /> <br /> I'm assuming this is for a player - and I just really like open ended tests and scenarios. They're IMO far better ways of testing someone's mettle, especially since the solar will know that this is still all a test... albeit one that also heavily emphases basic survival as well, which is a key lunar trait.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T17:35:34-07:00","id":1128637,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the suggestions - after writing this post I took the scenario in a slightly different direction. The solars were set on a path to clean up one of the messes left by their first age incarnations - very specific to my game, but could be easily modified to fit elsewhere.<br /> <br /> In my game, I made it that one of the circle's first age incarnations was involved in the creation of the Brass Legion. A twilight sorcerer-tyrant who ruled over nations of mortals with an iron (well, brass) fist.<br /> <br /> The character died in the early stages of the usurpation, but they had been in the middle of clearing out of one location where their work had led to a severe corruption by demons, and they were moving all their stuff to another location before sealing off a tainted manse. <br /> <br /> For story reasons, the solar had two lion dogs as attendants, and the lion dogs had been charged with taking 1000 of the brass legionaries to a hiding spot deep in the desert and waiting for the solar to arrive and claim them.<br /> <br /> The solar was killed, and so the lion dogs waited. And waited. And waited. By the time they emerged, the contagion and the fair-folk crusade had forever changed the landscape of the world they had known, and there were no solars to be found. After a bit more waiting, the lion dogs, loyal to their dead master, started trying to revive the brass legions and using them to rebuild the empire they knew their master would expect to see upon their eventual reincarnation.<br /> <br /> While some of the legionaries had the ability to repair themselves and others, they lacked the resources or tools necessary to maintain them indefinitely. So they activated only a small number at a time (which was also difficult because the control mechanisms were made for human hands, not giant paws).<br /> <br /> The dogs slowly manipulated local populations and elevated mortal leaders in status, to the point where they could be trusted to be given access to the brass legion and shown some of the basic commands - the humans were never fully instructed and only told how to program the legionaries to give commands the lion dogs wanted them to have. <br /> <br /> Fast forward 500 years, and you have an Egyptian-styled civlisation where the leaders are elevated to a status of demi-god because of their association with the lion dogs and association with the brass legionaries, and, modeled after their solar master's tyranny, they have enslaved neighboring populations to serve the original population - a strong caste system develops, and life is generally pretty shitty for the tens of thousands of people who are enslaved by this civilisation. <br /> <br /> The characters get dropped into a situation where the abuse of slaves is apparent. WHatever they do, and however they work their way through the layers of the society will ultimately bring them into contact with the god-king who is the puppet of the lion dogs. <br /> <br /> When the lion dogs see the solars, they recognise the reincarnated shard of their former master and say &quot;You're back at last, here, take control of this civlisation we've built in your name and honour&quot;<br /> <br /> The test comes from what happens next.<br /> <br /> Everyone is a victim, to some degree. Even the ruling caste have been manipulated by the Lion Dogs who have been corrupted by their former solar master. There's no 'easy way out' and the way the PCs address the situation will give the Lunar some indication of their values and tendencies.<br /> <br /> Personally, knowing my players, I kind of expect the Lunar to view them as potential enemies after they kill/defeat the lion dogs and possibly their puppet ruler, take control of the reins of power, 'free' the slaves but expect them to keep working as they had been but for pay instead of, well, slavery and possibly deal with dissent form the ruling caste by banishing or executing them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Visit me at <a href=\"http://www.bragrman.com\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Tales of Grey</i></a> - my RPG Game-Master's blog.<br /> <br /> &quot;If only I had an enemy bigger than my apathy, I could have won&quot; - <i>I gave you all,</i> Mumford &amp; Sons","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8520-capitantypo","name":"CapitanTypo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8520_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"896"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}